body:
## Product-Owner directive

Complete the QIK-VRT system by preserving the full e-mail infrastructure lineage, beginning with the first direct Internet e-mail received in Germany at Karlsruhe and continuing through contemporary cloud variants.

## Historical anchor

The implementation must preserve the exact qualified claim:

- received at Karlsruhe on 3 August 1984 at 10:14 local time;
- sent by Laura Breeden on 2 August 1984 at 12:35 US local time from the CSNET Coordination and Information Center at BBN in Boston;
- addressed to Werner Zorn and Michael Rotert as `zorn@germany.csnet` and `rotert@germany.csnet`;
- routed via CSNET infrastructure and manually retrieved from the relay;
- this was the first direct Internet e-mail to a separate e-mail server accessible throughout Germany, not the first use of electronic messages of every kind in Germany.

Primary historical sources:

- https://www.kit.edu/kit/english/pi_2009_090.php
- https://www.kit.edu/kit/english/pi_2014_15153.php

## Required protocol lineage

Preserve and separate at least:

1. ARPANET/CSNET and RFC 822-era messaging;
2. SMTP transfer and relay;
3. DNS MX routing, UUCP and X.400 gateway history;
4. MIME content, POP3 retrieval and IMAP synchronization;
5. message submission, TLS-first access/transport and SMTPUTF8;
6. SPF, DKIM and DMARC domain authentication boundaries;
7. JMAP synchronization, search, submission and push;
8. self-hosted, hosted, managed, serverless, API-first, event-stream, hybrid and edge/cloud mail variants;
9. Google Workspace/Gmail, Microsoft 365/Exchange Online, AWS SES, Cloudflare Email Service and standards-based JMAP adapter classes without embedding provider credentials or transferring authority.

## QIK-VRT invariants

```text
RFC5321_ENVELOPE != RFC5322_CONTENT
SMTP_250 != MAILBOX_STORED
MAILBOX_STORED != CLIENT_SYNCHRONIZED
CLIENT_SYNCHRONIZED != RENDERED
RENDERED != HUMAN_READ
READ_RECEIPT != EFFECT_ACK
WEBHOOK_NOTIFICATION != MAILBOX_DELTA
SPF_DKIM_DMARC != NATURAL_PERSON_AUTHENTICATION
TLS_TRANSPORT != END_TO_END_CONTENT_CONFIDENTIALITY
M68000_ROUTE_DECISION != NETWORK_EFFECT
```

Regular polling is not an admissible operating mode. Provider events, webhooks, push notifications and queue deliveries drive domain work. Bounded watch/subscription renewal may maintain leases only; detected cursor/history gaps trigger exact delta reconciliation.

## First executable tranche

Create a current-main-bound history-preserving candidate containing:

- normative machine-readable e-mail infrastructure policy;
- complete lineage and cloud-variant inventory;
- host-adapter registry;
- finite Motorola 68000 route-decision microkernel with exhaustive reference equivalence and D3 preservation;
- append-only receipt and Effect-Acknowledgement boundaries;
- focused tests and event-driven exact-head workflow;
- Product-Owner work-unit receipt.

## Completion boundary

This issue does not itself send e-mail, change MX records, create cloud accounts, obtain credentials, accept provider terms, expose mailbox content, claim natural-person authentication, or establish production availability. Each provider adapter and each external effect remains separately credential-bound, exact-artifact-bound and post-effect reobserved.

```text
PASS = NOT_CLAIMED
FINAL_PASS = NOT_CLAIMED
EFFECT_ACK_DONE = NOT_CLAIMED
```
